---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---
<BaseLayout title="Barcode API Pricing | BarcodeNest" description="Compare Creator barcode generation at $4.99/month, product lookup plans and one-time lookup packs. Each service has its own account-wide allowance." current="pricing">
  <header class="page-hero"><div class="container"><div class="eyebrow">Workspace and API pricing</div><h1>Choose a creation or product data plan.</h1><p class="lede">Create barcode images and labels with Creator for $4.99/month. Choose Starter or Growth for product lookup integrations and larger tool allowances.</p></div></header>
  <section class="section"><div class="container"><article class="plan"><span class="plan-tag">Barcode creation</span><h2 id="creator">Creator</h2><div class="price">$4.99 <small>/ month</small></div><p>A monthly package for barcode images and printable labels.</p><ul><li>1,000 generated images per month</li><li>250 printable labels per month, including copies</li><li>ZIP batches of up to 25 images</li><li>EAN-13, UPC-A, Code 128 and QR</li><li>SVG, 300-DPI PNG and PDF label output</li><li>Website and API access · 120 requests/minute</li><li>Product lookups: 0 · CSV enrichment rows: 0</li></ul><a class="button button-signal" href="/billing/?plan=CREATOR&amp;interval=month">Choose Creator · $4.99/month</a><p>Monthly billing. Creation allowances reset on the first day of each month at 00:00 UTC. Signup is required.</p></article></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="container"><article class="plan"><span class="plan-tag">One-time · No subscription</span><h2 id="one-time">500-call pack</h2><div class="price">$4.99 <small>once</small></div><p>500 calls valid for 30 days from activation after confirmed payment. No automatic renewal.</p><ul><li>30 requests / minute</li><li>Buy another pack at any time</li><li>Each purchase has its own 30-day expiry; earliest-expiring calls are used first</li><li>Unused calls expire; buying more does not extend an older pack</li><li>Free lifetime credits stay separate</li></ul><a class="button button-signal" href="/billing/?plan=ONE_TIME">Buy 500 calls</a><p>Available to Free and one-time accounts. Existing Starter and Growth subscriptions remain separate. One valid single lookup or each submitted batch barcode uses one call, including missing products.</p></article></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="container">
    <div class="pricing-switcher billing-toggle" role="group" aria-label="Pricing cadence"><button class="is-active" type="button" data-pricing-toggle="month" aria-pressed="true">Monthly</button><button type="button" data-pricing-toggle="year" aria-pressed="false">Yearly <span>Save 20%</span></button></div>
    <div class="pricing-grid">
    <article class="plan"><span class="plan-tag">Evaluate coverage</span><h3>Free</h3><div class="price">$0</div><ul><li>250 lifetime successful-result credits</li><li>30 requests / minute</li><li>Single and batch barcode lookups</li><li>Dashboard and key management</li></ul><a class="button button-signal" href="/register">Get API Key</a></article>
    <article class="plan featured"><span class="plan-tag">Starter · Small integrations</span><h3>Starter</h3><p>2,000 API calls / month</p><div class="price" data-monthly="$9.99|/ month" data-yearly="$7.99|/ month">$9.99 <small>/ month</small></div><p class="annual-total" hidden>Billed $95.90 yearly</p><ul><li>300 requests / minute</li><li>Monthly usage tracking</li><li>API key management</li><li>Email support</li></ul><a class="button button-signal" data-paid-plan="STARTER" href="/billing/?plan=STARTER&amp;interval=month">Choose Starter</a></article>
    <article class="plan"><span class="plan-tag">Growth · More volume</span><h3>Growth</h3><p>5,000 API calls / month</p><div class="price" data-monthly="$19.99|/ month" data-yearly="$15.99|/ month">$19.99 <small>/ month</small></div><p class="annual-total" hidden>Billed $191.90 yearly</p><ul><li>1,200 requests / minute</li><li>Monthly usage tracking</li><li>API key management</li><li>Email support</li></ul><a class="button" data-paid-plan="GROWTH" href="/billing/?plan=GROWTH&amp;interval=month">Choose Growth</a></article>
  </div><div class="callout"><strong>Usage accounting:</strong> Free accounts receive 250 lifetime credits: each matched barcode result consumes one credit, including each matched result in a batch. Existing recorded usage counts toward the lifetime allowance. Paid plans count valid single lookup attempts and each submitted batch barcode as one unit, including missing products. Authentication failures, health checks, and account pages do not consume allowance. Failed lookups consume no Free credits. Annual subscriptions are billed yearly; API allowances reset monthly.</div></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="narrow"><h2>Which plan fits your workload?</h2><p>Free is 250 lifetime successful-result credits, not a monthly allowance. For occasional work, buy a $4.99 pack of 500 calls; each pack expires after 30 days and does not renew. Recurring plans suit sustained use.</p><p>Use Free to validate a representative sample. Choose Starter when you need up to 2,000 monthly lookups or a higher request rate than Free. Choose Growth for up to 5,000 monthly lookups or bursts up to 1,200 requests/minute. All tiers use the same product index; upgrading increases allowances, not product coverage.</p><p>For example, 1,000 successful single-product requests use 1,000 paid calls. Each submitted barcode consumes one paid lookup unit.</p><h2>How do I buy a paid plan?</h2><p>Choose Creator, Starter or Growth above, sign in or create an account, and review the selected plan in Billing. Payment starts only when you explicitly continue to secure checkout.</p><h2>What should I check before upgrading?</h2><p>Test coverage and required fields with your actual products. Review <a href="/data/">data sources</a> and <a href="/terms/">data-use terms</a>. Product matches, images, and field completeness vary. For workflows, see <a href="/barcode-api-for-inventory/">inventory integrations</a> and <a href="/product-data-api/">catalog enrichment</a>.</p><h2>Need more than 5,000 calls per month?</h2><p><a href="/contact/">Contact us with your expected monthly volume and request rate</a> before choosing a plan.</p></div></section>
  <section class="cta-band"><div class="container cta-grid"><div><div class="eyebrow">Free developer tier</div><h2>Create your account and make the first request.</h2></div><div class="hero-actions"><a class="button button-signal" href="/register">Get Free API Key</a><a class="button" href="/docs">Documentation</a></div></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="container"><h2>Workspace capacity and separate tool allowances</h2><p><a href="/vault/">Your private Vault</a> stores products, collections, notes, prices and custom fields. Storage capacity does not reset monthly. New Creator accounts receive 500 records; existing accounts retain their current capacity, shown in My Workspace. Reading and editing saved products consumes no lookup credits. If you downgrade above your new capacity, existing records remain accessible; remove records or upgrade before adding more. Prices support USD, EUR and GBP. CSV exports preserve source values, but spreadsheet imports should treat barcode columns as Text.</p><p>Product lookup, image scanning, image generation, printable labels and CSV enrichment each have their own allowance. Tool units are shared across your account's API keys and reset on the first day of each month at 00:00 UTC.</p><div class="comparison-scroll" role="region" aria-label="Service plan comparison" tabindex="0"><table class="status-table"><thead><tr><th>Service / storage capacity</th><th>Free / One-time</th><th>Creator</th><th>Starter</th><th>Growth</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th>Saved Vault products (capacity)</th><td>25</td><td>500</td><td>2,000</td><td>10,000</td></tr><tr><th>Vault CSV / JSON export</th><td>—</td><td>Included</td><td>Included</td><td>Included</td></tr><tr><th>Saved label templates</th><td>—</td><td>10</td><td>25</td><td>100</td></tr><tr><th>Generated SKUs / month</th><td>—</td><td>1,000</td><td>5,000</td><td>20,000</td></tr><tr><th>Bulk processing rows / month</th><td>—</td><td>1,000</td><td>5,000</td><td>20,000</td></tr><tr><th>Image scans</th><td>50</td><td>500</td><td>2,000</td><td>5,000</td></tr><tr><th>Generated images</th><td>100</td><td>1,000</td><td>2,000</td><td>10,000</td></tr><tr><th>ZIP batch generation</th><td>Single images</td><td>25 images / request</td><td>25 images / request</td><td>100 images / request</td></tr><tr><th>Printable labels</th><td>25</td><td>250</td><td>500</td><td>2,500</td></tr><tr><th>CSV enrichment rows</th><td>250</td><td>0</td><td>2,000</td><td>5,000</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>One accepted scan image (including no-match results), one generated image, one printed label including copies, or one enrichment input row consumes one unit in that category. All barcode tools require an account. CSV preview consumes no units. Website generation and API generation each consume one image unit per image. One-time lookup packs provide the Free tool allowances.</p><p><a href="/barcode-scanner/">Scan a barcode</a>, <a href="/barcode-generator/">try the generator</a>, <a href="/barcode-labels/">print labels</a>, or <a href="/csv-product-enrichment/">enrich a CSV</a>. See the <a href="/docs/barcode-tools/">tool API reference</a> for details.</p></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
<script>
  type Interval = "month" | "year";
  function selectPricing(interval: Interval) {
    document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>("[data-pricing-toggle]").forEach((button) => { const active = button.dataset.pricingToggle === interval; button.classList.toggle("is-active", active); button.setAttribute("aria-pressed", String(active)); });
    document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>(".price[data-monthly]").forEach((price) => { const [amount, cadence] = (interval === "year" ? price.dataset.yearly : price.dataset.monthly)!.split("|"); price.innerHTML = `${amount} <small>${cadence}</small>`; });
    document.querySelectorAll<HTMLAnchorElement>("[data-paid-plan]").forEach((link) => { link.href = `/billing/?plan=${link.dataset.paidPlan}&interval=${interval}`; });
    document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>(".annual-total").forEach((note) => note.hidden = interval !== "year");
  }
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>("[data-pricing-toggle]").forEach((button) => button.addEventListener("click", () => selectPricing(button.dataset.pricingToggle as Interval)));
</script>
